# Global ignores, wired to core.excludesfile by git/install.sh.
#
# Only genuinely universal junk belongs here. Anything a repo might reasonably
# want to commit stays out, because a global ignore is invisible from inside the
# repo and silently drops new files.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: the .agent/ artifact directory (and its legacy name
# .evolve/). A survey of 84 local repos found 51 of them tracking .evolve/ on
# purpose — pursuits, reflections, and scorecards are part of those repos'
# record. Ten repos in the blueprint-agent family also keep a checked-in
# .agent/workflows/. Ignoring either globally would make new files there vanish
# from git status with no local .gitignore line to explain why. Repos that do
# treat these as scratch already carry their own .gitignore entry.

